        {"h2_html": "In commercial real estate, the deal is the relationship you kept <em>warm for years</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">A tenant whose lease comes up in three years, an investor who buys once every few years, a landlord you meet today who will not list until next spring: the broker who is still in front of them when the timing finally arrives is the one who wins the deal, and it is rarely the one with the sharpest pitch. It is the one who stayed in touch. Commercial real estate runs on a longer clock than almost any business, and the place where money is lost is not a missed call, it is the contact you met once, meant to follow up with, and never did.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">A CRM keeps every one of those relationships in front of you and follows up on a schedule you set, with the market notes and check-ins that keep your name familiar over a cycle measured in months and years. The landlord, the tenant, and the investor hear from you at the right moments instead of forgetting you exist, and the deal comes back to you when it is finally live.</p>'},
