        {"h2_html": "A lease expiration is a follow-up date <em>in disguise</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">The most valuable dates in your pipeline are the ones nobody is watching. A tenant whose lease expires in eighteen months is a live opportunity today, not next year, because the search and the decision start long before the expiration. The CRM surfaces those dates for you and prompts the outreach at the moment it matters, so you are the broker who called first with a plan, not the one who found out after the tenant already renewed or moved. Between those milestones, steady and light touches, a market update, a relevant listing, a quick check-in, keep you familiar without you having to remember every name and date.</p>'},
